# ax web UI — modals for forms and edit screens

> **ABSOLUTE**: Create, edit, and multi-field configuration flows MUST NOT render as inline page sections. They open in a **centered modal** with a **blurred backdrop**.

## When this applies

Any new or changed UI under `crates/ax-web/web-ui/` that:

- Creates a new entity (profile, memory, rule, skill, workspace, …)
- Edits an existing entity via a form
- Collects multi-field user input (more than one control in a flow)

This rule is matched automatically when prompts mention forms, modals, edit screens, or new screens in the web UI.

## Required pattern

Use `ModalShell` from `components/ModalShell.tsx`:

```text
1. Page shows a trigger button only (e.g. "Add profile", "New memory", "Edit")
2. Modal overlay: position fixed, inset 0, semi-transparent backdrop, backdrop-filter: blur(4px)
3. Centered panel: title, optional subtitle, form body, footer with Cancel + primary action
4. Close on Esc, backdrop click (outside panel), and Cancel
5. document.body overflow hidden while open
6. createPortal(..., document.body) so modals sit above the app shell
```

## Allowed inline (no modal)

- Single-row `SettingRow` controls on Settings (one select, one toggle)
- Read-only list + detail split panes (Nodes, Memory list, Files tree)
- Full-page primary views routed via hash when the entire page *is* the editor (Policy rule/skill page in view mode)

## Forbidden

- Inline expandable form blocks that push page content down (accordion create/edit sections)
- "Add …" flows embedded in card body without a modal
- Modals without blurred backdrop
- Reporting form UI work complete without using `ModalShell` or equivalent shared overlay classes (`.ax-modal-overlay`)

## Reference implementations

- `components/ModalShell.tsx` — shared form modal wrapper
- `components/ProjectBrowserModal.tsx` — browse/switch dialog (same overlay pattern)
- `components/AgentsSettingsSection.tsx` — Add profile modal
- `components/agent/ProfileEditor.tsx` — Edit profile modal
- `pages/Memory.tsx` — New memory modal

## With web-ui changes

Follow `web-ui-rebuild` — rebuild and reinstall `ax` before handoff.
